# Secrets.
#
# `lib/core/config/env.dart` documents .env as "the git-ignored `.env` file",
# but no .gitignore existed, so nothing enforced that. .env now carries DB_SALT
# — the salt for the SQLCipher key derivation — and .env.example exists to be
# committed in its place.
.env
.test
.docs
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated from .env by `dart run tool/generate_ios_env.dart`; carries the
# Google Maps key that SECURITY.md §9 keeps out of git history.
ios/Flutter/Env.xcconfig

# Note: build/ and .dart_tool/ are deliberately NOT listed here. This repo
# already tracks files under both, so ignoring them now would only hide further
# changes without untracking what is committed. Removing them is a separate,
# deliberate cleanup:
#   git rm -r --cached build .dart_tool
# Flutter / Dart build artifacts
.dart_tool/
build/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.pub-cache/
.pub/

# iOS build artifacts
ios/Pods/
ios/Runner.xcworkspace
.DS_Store

# Graphify knowledge graph (rebuildable artifact: `graphify update .`)
graphify-out/

# Envied output. Deliberately the ONE generated file that is not committed:
# unlike the drift *.g.dart files, it embeds the obfuscated SAP gateway URL and
# the database salt. Obfuscation is defense-in-depth, not a secret store
# (docs/skills/security.md §4), so it is regenerated at build time instead.
lib/core/config/env.g.dart

# Machine-specific Claude Code settings: the graphify PreToolUse hooks embed an
# ABSOLUTE path to the executable, which differs per OS and per user. Committing
# them breaks every other developer's machine, so each developer generates their
# own with `graphify claude install`. See docs/GRAPHIFY.md.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Firebase per-app config. Not high-severity secrets — they ship inside the
# binary — but they name the project and its API keys, and
# `docs/feature/notification/notification-mobile.md` Step 1 asks for them to be
# kept out of the repo.
#
# ⚠️ BOTH FILES ARE STILL TRACKED, so these two lines currently do nothing:
# .gitignore does not affect a file git already follows. Untracking them is a
# deliberate, coordinated change — every developer and the CI runner has to
# obtain them out of band first, or the Android build fails at
# `processDebugGoogleServices` and iOS silently loses its Firebase config.
#
# To complete it, once the team has the files distributed:
#     git rm --cached android/app/google-services.json \
#                     ios/Runner/GoogleService-Info.plist
#
# These entries are here so a fresh copy is not re-added by accident the moment
# that happens.
android/app/google-services.json
ios/Runner/GoogleService-Info.plist

# Kotlin compile-daemon session markers. Empty, per-machine, recreated on every
# Gradle run — and one was accidentally committed in `feat: notification
# integration` because this directory was not ignored.
android/.kotlin/
